also because of V5's suggestion that they're actually still up to their old tricks and not remotely affected by the Sabbat's current degeneration into football hooliganery. They're just sitting back and relaxing in their bunker according to Justin Achilli and waiting out Gehenna as the cannon fodder does the dying for them. If they've managed to weather the storm now, I could easily see them as the person who did this in the past.<br /> <br /> Mr. Vykos is a natural survivor as shown by his abilty to adapt and learn new skills and that was something his great grand sire The Dracon was known for as shown by his write up in Constaniople By Night.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T14:48:39-08:00","id":1500532,"title":"","content":"Yay! We're back in business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T18:07:57-08:00","id":1500553,"title":"","content":"I think my only issue is the idea that all of this was centrally planned. Rather than an &quot;organic&quot; shift over centuries, as Sabbat thought leaders made ad hoc changes to further the sect's interests. There doesn't need to be a conspiracy, when, to quote Ross Scott from Accursed Farms, &quot;ruthless rich people tend to think alike&quot;. (Just replace &quot;rich&quot; with &quot;vampirically powerful&quot;).<br /> <br /> But I do like the central concept of the Roads being systematically perverted over time to serve the interests of those in power. I especially like framing the Path of Caine as a sham religion. It's a theological framework invented whole cloth to retroactively justify the kind of violence and bellicosity that a forever-war demands. Which will keep the Sabbat populace wound up and unwilling to even entertain the concept of diplomacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T21:50:53-08:00","id":1500577,"title":"","content":"Cool ideas.<br /> <br /> The only thing I didn't really like all that much was how Roads and Paths could be so easily created and manipulated. A I've understood the Roads and Paths these requires ALOT of hard work to follow and convert to. While the concept of manipulation of Paths and Paths as sham religions and such fits some Vampire themes very well I think it on the other hand it sells the Beast as a threat a bit short.<br /> <br /> But this is just my perspective and I make no claim as to be an expert on Roads and Paths or VtM and DA lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T10:20:30-08:00","id":1500619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1500553#post1500553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my only issue is the idea that all of this was centrally planned. Rather than an &quot;organic&quot; shift over centuries, as Sabbat thought leaders made ad hoc changes to further the sect's interests. There doesn't need to be a conspiracy, when, to quote Ross Scott from Accursed Farms, &quot;ruthless rich people tend to think alike&quot;. (Just replace &quot;rich&quot; with &quot;vampirically powerful&quot;).<br /> <br /> But I do like the central concept of the Roads being systematically perverted over time to serve the interests of those in power. I especially like framing the Path of Caine as a sham religion. It's a theological framework invented whole cloth to retroactively justify the kind of violence and bellicosity that a forever-war demands. Which will keep the Sabbat populace wound up and unwilling to even entertain the concept of diplomacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I suppose it would be the question of what would make the better story. The Sabbat evolving naturally over time is certainly something that would be realistic but part of the conceit of V:TM is that the undead are genius political manipulators and planners that are always doing puppet master-like things behind the scenes with their actions under the control of someone higher than them in the chain.<br /> <br /> The funny thing about the Path of Caine is that I'm pretty sure it being a sham religion designed to make canon fodder is canon. So much of it is from the Path of Blood and the Path of Blood was never going to be taught to outsiders. I remember, sadly not where, that they also established the Path of Caine was thus created as a compromise by the Assamite Antitribu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T13:36:53-08:00","id":1500646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1500577#post1500577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool ideas.<br /> <br /> The only thing I didn't really like all that much was how Roads and Paths could be so easily created and manipulated. A I've understood the Roads and Paths these requires ALOT of hard work to follow and convert to. While the concept of manipulation of Paths and Paths as sham religions and such fits some Vampire themes very well I think it on the other hand it sells the Beast as a threat a bit short.<br /> <br /> But this is just my perspective and I make no claim as to be an expert on Roads and Paths or VtM and DA lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could actually be a selling point depending on how cynical you want to be with the Sabbat. One of the things that was common in Revised was the idea that most Sabbat vampires on Paths have 1-5 dots in their Paths versus having the kind of incredibly high scores you'd think something that would be better suited to vampirism would give you. In this respect, most Sabbat vampires by following the &quot;artificial&quot; Paths are unwittingly crippling themselves spiritually because the teachings are designed to put the Sect above actual enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T21:04:04-08:00","id":1500696,"title":"","content":"I see the Paths/Roads as being inherently artificial and constructed, with the possible exception of Humanity and Beast. They don't really exist to provide a vampire any kind of spiritial enlightenment, though it might do so incidentally. It's there to provide a mental, emotional, and behavioral framework for moderating the vampire in relation to their Beast. It's a bulwark against the part of themselves that would, if it had its way, dive straight into atavistic indulgence of every urge, desire, or whim, regardless of utility. To adopt a Road or Path is to draw a line in the sand and say &quot;this far, and no further&quot;. Where that line is drawn depends on the Road/Path.<br /> <br /> As such, it's entirely reasonable for a Path to be wholly artificial by intent, and still function as a bulwark against the Beast. It provides a code of ethics the vampire unlives by, and gives them a purpose above and beyond mindless, selfish indulgence. Even if, depending on the Path/Road, the vampire does a lot of indulging anyway. This greater purpose might be Pro-Social Altruism (Humanity), Honor (Chivalry/Honorable Accord), Lordship (Kings/Power &amp; The Inner Voice), or One's Infernal Masters (Devil/Evil Revelations).<br /> <br /> If a vampire's greater purpose is &quot;Caine and the study thereof&quot; - or the sect-serving vision of Caine - it doesn't invalidate it as a tool for forestalling Wassail. At least for a vampire's mental health, it doesn't exactly matter if that tool is founded on bullshit and lies. As Mage demonstrates, people adopt belief systems that serve a purpose in their lives. People can go their entire lives confidently assured in a worldview, without ever being bothered about it not once being true. It only becomes a problem, Cognitive Dissonance wise, when pesky reality starts to intrude on the lie they adopted (or were sold or indoctrinated with). And people are very good at rationalizing or unconsciously forgetting contradictions in their worldview.<br /> <br /> For vampires, so long as the Road/Path keeps them above water, it functions as intended. For adherents to the Path of Caine, it helps that there's centuries of other vampires who, knowingly or not, contributed to a body of Noddist &quot;lore&quot; that maintains the lie of their philosophy. A modern Noddist can go just as many centuries without being tangibly confronted with the artificiality of their doctrine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T22:23:37-08:00","id":1500702,"title":"","content":"I've always preffered the idea the Sabbat and paths works as it's supposed too, it just happens to be horrifying because of its vampire supremecist attitudes. This is a good angle if you want to explore the anarch origins of the Sabbat however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T08:34:28-08:00","id":1500843,"title":"","content":"Just echoing the points brought up by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a>. While I do see a path being created for the express purpose of making a sect more controllable, like the path of the Hive, the reason Paths/Roads exist are more for the rules and codes that help bind the beast and stave of Wassail. If those codes and rules also are part of the spirituality of the sect, like the setite paths, then its all the better for it.<br /> <br /> I find it interesting to include Mon\u00e7ada as part of that list, mostly because of how he views religion in specific. Mon\u00e7ada despised the Cainite Heresy and its ideas, him moving to make a Church of Caine and a sham religion when he views the House of God to be paramount is a bit strange. I don't think he would be involved with that since he always sought to destroy what he view as an abomination to God.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T16:09:19-08:00","id":1500877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1500843#post1500843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just echoing the points brought up by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a>. While I do see a path being created for the express purpose of making a sect more controllable, like the path of the Hive, the reason Paths/Roads exist are more for the rules and codes that help bind the beast and stave of Wassail. If those codes and rules also are part of the spirituality of the sect, like the setite paths, then its all the better for it.<br /> <br /> I find it interesting to include Mon\u00e7ada as part of that list, mostly because of how he views religion in specific. Mon\u00e7ada despised the Cainite Heresy and its ideas, him moving to make a Church of Caine and a sham religion when he views the House of God to be paramount is a bit strange. I don't think he would be involved with that since he always sought to destroy what he view as an abomination to God.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I in fact mention how strange it is for him to be and that was why I included him. Because in the WOD, I think you always need someone acting out of character sometimes because:<br /> <br /> 1. Vampires are innately hypocritical and will often do something against seemingly deeply held principles for power or control<br /> <br /> 2. They're not fully of their right mind when doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T17:04:40-08:00","id":1500882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1500696#post1500696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see the Paths/Roads as being inherently artificial and constructed, with the possible exception of Humanity and Beast. They don't really exist to provide a vampire any kind of spiritial enlightenment, though it might do so incidentally. It's there to provide a mental, emotional, and behavioral framework for moderating the vampire in relation to their Beast. It's a bulwark against the part of themselves that would, if it had its way, dive straight into atavistic indulgence of every urge, desire, or whim, regardless of utility.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is how I have always seen the Paths too. They have nothing to do with &quot;enlightenment&quot; in its ordinary sense. It is not necessarily spiritual (though they can be). They exist for one purpose only - to provide a means for the vampire to control their Beast so it does not take them over. Incidentally, I think the Path of Humanity is the same thing. It is equally artificial as any other Path. Its big merit is that it is more natural as it is based on how vampires acted when they were alive.<br /> <br /> The essence of a path is that provides a vampire with the framework of self-discipline of controlling the Beast. If it doesn't do the job of disciplining the vampire to deny the Beast's instincts, it is useless. So every Path needs reasons why its followers would choose not to kill, not to feed when hungry, not to lash out at danger, etc. It needs to provide reasons why the intellectual mind is in charge and denying the Beast's attempts to take over. It needs to be very well developed, consistent, and comprehensive because the Beast will easily take over if there are any significant gaps in the system. If the Path does not at some level force the vampire to deny the Beast on a somewhat consistent basis, I don't think it is working as it needs to do. A Path doesn't need to constrain the Beast in the same way that Humanity does, but it still needs to force the intellect to actively control the Beast and make it subservient. <br /> <br /> A philosophy of &quot;life&quot; (or unliving) could be logically consistent, but unless it is somehow able to make the Beast subservient to the vampire's rational mind, it can't be a Path. (One reason perhaps the vampire Path of Humanity is a more &quot;modern&quot; than classical understanding was perhaps the need for a more universal and consistent approach as &quot;I only act moral towards my in-group, and can treat outsiders however I feel like&quot; easily lets the Beast take over).<br /> <br /> Do the Paths as written in the game actually do this? I would say many Paths fail at this. Many of the original Paths in 2e were very bad and derided as &quot;the path that allows me to do whatever I want.&quot; Things did improve in Revised, but not all paths were equally well designed. I'd have to reread the Paths before I could name individual Paths that I feel don't work. I also don't play Sabbat games so I have little experience at seeing how well it plays out.<br /> <br /> I do like Paths as it allows characters to act like the villainous vampires of popular media (pre-Anne Rice) and violate Humanity without them immediately descending into Wassail. The game needs that. It is just that some Paths still need various amounts of work to get each one to where it needs to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T22:35:08-08:00","id":1500899,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much how I view it as well. Every vampires deals with the berzerk urge to feed to gluttony, and to kill whenever even slightly angry. Each path must therefore have a reason why the vampire doesn't give into those two major berzerker urges.<br /> <br /> Humanity-&quot;I will not feed to gluttony when even slightly hungry or kill when slightly angry, because that is a betrayal of the human race which I still consider myself a member of, albeit a cursed member.&quot;<br /> <br /> Feral Heart-&quot;I will not feed to gluttony when even slightly hungry or kill when slightly angry because that is a threat to the survival of cunning, clear-sighted, and eternal predator I aspire to be.&quot;<br /> <br /> Honorable Accord-&quot;I will not feed to gluttony when even slightly hungry, or kill when slightly angry, because that threatens the pack and sect to which I have sworn a sacred oath of allegiance.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cathari-.....yeah, I don't get how Cathari works, never have, that's part of why I've had that Path declared heretical and genocided in my Sabbat games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T01:18:17-08:00","id":1500907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1500899#post1500899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cathari-.....yeah, I don't get how Cathari works, never have, that's part of why I've had that Path declared heretical and genocided in my Sabbat games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;I am an entity of sin, i accept that the beast is a part of me and will indulge myself.....to a degree.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T01:30:18-08:00","id":1500908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1500899#post1500899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cathari-.....yeah, I don't get how Cathari works, never have, that's part of why I've had that Path declared heretical and genocided in my Sabbat games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends on how you figure dealing with the Beast works.<br /> <br /> In my games, Path of Cathari are wild hedonists who drink when they're thirsty, fuck when they're horny, and sleep when they're sleepy. The are usually too stoned and drunk to want to give into the raw animalism of the beast. So it works basically the same way as the Path of the Beast. You give in enough that the Beast doesn't overwhelm you because it's pretty okay with the way things are presently going. You don't clamp it down to such a degree that it's trying to explode outward.<br /> <br /> Of course, in my games, this is the Low Level Path of Cathari.<br /> <br /> Once you hit 5-10, you start getting less into fucking and eating because it's fun and more like, &quot;fucking and eating are gateways to transcendence with the True God of Caine.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T05:24:40-08:00","id":1500920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1500908#post1500908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it depends on how you figure dealing with the Beast works.<br /> <br /> In my games, Path of Cathari are wild hedonists who drink when they're thirsty, fuck when they're horny, and sleep when they're sleepy. The are usually too stoned and drunk to want to give into the raw animalism of the beast. So it works basically the same way as the Path of the Beast. You give in enough that the Beast doesn't overwhelm you because it's pretty okay with the way things are presently going. You don't clamp it down to such a degree that it's trying to explode outward.<br /> <br /> Of course, in my games, this is the Low Level Path of Cathari.<br /> <br /> Once you hit 5-10, you start getting less into fucking and eating because it's fun and more like, &quot;fucking and eating are gateways to transcendence with the True God of Caine.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much yeah,if you look at cathari sins it's actually quite restrictive in terms of behavoir. You may be able to do horrible things but theirs a lot you explicitly can't do and you're expected to be a proactive agent of sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T06:25:37-08:00","id":1500933,"title":"","content":"I would like to imagine the Paths taking the forefront and turning into fanatical zeal, as in V5, as either a very deliberate result of this conspiracy. For now they have a resolute and tight-knitted army of Cainite soldiers. Or as a terrible consequence from all the manipulation, which alienated many, pushed-off more individualist and grounded vamps, and made the Sabbat disperse, in many cultish cells that rage a short-sighted savage war, faded to fail and wane.<br /> <br /> But that is the funny thing right. The Sabbat has very material and political goals. Destruction of their opponents and targets, as matter of principle. Antediluvians have to die, not only they deserve it, but it is either the ancients or the Sabbat that has to go. So Paths aren't really ideologies that should be followed until the end, pursued and evolved by the faithful. Because spiritual transcendence isn't the sect's goal, not really. They aren't monks, consecrated souls searching for heaven. They are holy crusaders, seeking to end the evil in the world, and take their rightful place as the chosen. So it makes lot of sense to make Paths, unlike Roads, more pragmatic, war-aligned, useful to the cause. Which would give a fun hook for some Sabbats to think 'hey, this seems weird right? the Path principle is thus X, but what the priest says is Y' and then having some members go in search of the &quot;original truths&quot; of the Path, and the Sabbat Inquisition or Black Hand be like &quot;don't go there, son; I'll have to take you out&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T12:05:36-08:00","id":1500955,"title":"","content":"I think there are several major threads that eventually caused the Sabbat to become the organization it is today. None of the single threads could have done it alone, but the combination of all of them plus other decisions turned a bunch of Anarchs into the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> While the Anarchs who refused the Convention of Thorns are seen as the founders of the Sabbat, they clearly lacked almost all of the outstanding features of the Sabbat. The ones who refused were likely some of the most violent and criminal vampires who feared their crimes really would not be forgiven, and they'd be betrayed at some point. But others who refused were just idealists committed to an extreme of personal freedom who could not reconcile themselves to the Camarilla structure. So how this turned into some fanatical paramilitary organization dedicated to wiping out the antedeluvians and their servants requires some explanation.<br /> <br /> The creation of the Paths of Enlightenment is certainly one element of this, as some of the Paths were so monstrous it does not seem likely they could be incorporated into the Camarilla's Masquerade. But I think there are other important factors.<br /> <br /> One is the role of the Ravnos Methusaleh Vestgeir in saving the sect in its early days, and the subsequent belief that Vestgeir was Caine in disguise. If you adopt that view, then it seems providential and provides a legitimacy to your new sect that it did not have before. And I'm sure one of the Path of Caine's tenants is &quot;Vestgeir was Caine&quot;, which would be unqiue to the Sabbat and not necessarily something that a non-Sabbat on the Path would have adopted. As players/fans, we are given very little information about Vestgeir's time with the Sabbat and his actions and words. But in the Sabbat this would have to be very important and well known. However, because mentions of Vestgeir seem limited to the 2e Sabbat books and does not seem to be mentioned in Revised source material, he is often not known and therefore people don't consider the importance he had in the sect. (Personally, I find it funny to consider that much of the Sabbat culture might be a result of a Ravnos con job). In so far that the Anarchs who only wanted freedom became Sabbat obsessed about the Antedeluvians, I think Vestgeir must have played a very important role in that transformation.<br /> <br /> Another important thing to consider is the triumph of the &quot;conservatives&quot; over the Loyalists during the Second Sabbat Civil War that lead to the revised Code of Milan in 1933. This is what seems to have turned a very anarchic sect that consistently lost battles against the Camarilla over several centuries and kept fleeing to remote areas as a result, into the terrifying &quot;Sword of Caine&quot; that confronted the Camarilla in the 1990s. That centralized the sect and stripped away a lot of the Sabbat members' freedom. Many Sabbat embraced post-1933 likely do not even know about the way the Sabbat used to be unless they are in a Loyalist pack.<br /> <br /> Then of course there is the rise of Infernalism within the Sabbat, and the corresponding reaction against it that lead to the Sabbat Inquisition.<br /> <br /> I would include several important defections to the Sabbat that encouraged its transformation into a more centralized, war fighting organization. That would be Goratrix and and the Tremere anti-tribu, and the Serpents of the Light. Although these groups are small and lack influence on their own, their own high solidarity and internal leadership made them important assets to those forces. They had no allegiance to the Sabbat's original principles of freedom, and just wanted an organization that could protect them from their enemies. I don't think it is a surprise that Goratrix's defection happened around the time of the Sabbat civil wars, and the Tremere anti-tribu's aid was probably important to the eventual victory of the &quot;conservatives.&quot; And the Serpents defected in the 1960s after the triumph of the centralizers in the Third Sabbat Civil War. Neither group might want to see further consolidation, but they find the sect useful now in a way that the earlier sect might not be.<br /> <br /> Finally, if you go by Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, the True Black Hand's involvement in the sect caused a lot of this (even though their real target were the &quot;elders&quot; who defied the antedeluvians, not the antedeluvians themselves which they serve). The creation of the (false) Black Hand within the Sabbat did a lot to militarize it. Of course, Revised threw this all out and treated the entire Sabbat as if it were the (False) Black Hand. Given the controversy around DSotBH and wildly different fan opinion about it, it's hard to tell how important the True Black Hand's role is since every chronicle will likely have vastly different approaches to this material as canon for their chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T13:08:43-08:00","id":1500959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen#post1500430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Link:<a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2022/12/the-judas-compact-or-how-sabbat-got.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://unitedfederationofcharles.bl...abbat-got.html</a><br /> <br /> I thought I would share a recent article from my Sabbat games. I have a bit of a reputation as a Anarch fanboy (which is fair) but I actually love the Sword of Caine second-most among the undead. I absolutely love the spirituality, hypocrisy, and religious symbolism of the Black Hand. I've also done many Sabbat games where the characters are forced to try to reconcile all the various contradictory messages among its teachings.<br /> <br /> In Giovanni Chronicles II: Blood and Fire, the Black Monastery is introduced as a location where the Sabbat develops all of his paths. This is all Pre-Dark Ages and thus doesn't incorporate Roads of Enlightenment into the setting's history. Many of them are very similar to what the Sabbat will later follow but others are incredibly different, not insisting on their militant doctrines or the death cult's fanaticism. Quite a few are amoral by human standards but not overtly evil like the majority of Sabbat paths.<br /> <br /> While I, to be frank, dislike what was done with the Sabbat in Fifth Edition, I did actually think their sudden about-face on previously acceptable Sabbat practices fit with how I handled it in my games. The Sabbat is a religious organization and as we know from real life, there's always a conflict between the true believers, those using it for their own gain, and those who are somewhere in the middle.<br /> <br /> This is a bit of world-building about how I saw the Sabbat dealing with their own existential spiritual crisis.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Judas Compact</b></span><br /> <br /> The Judas Compact is created by <b>Sascha Vykos</b>, <b>Velya the Vivisectionist</b>, <b>Intisar the Setite</b>, and <b>Moncada</b> with several other high profile figures in the Sabbat's spiritual hierarchy. It is a primarily Lasombra and Tzimisce thing but a few other Antitribu (particularly Assamite) were invited as well. Those involved in it and capable of contributing found themselves blessed with the status of Pricius or Cardinalship in the Sabbat as well as permanently guaranteeing their position in the Sword of Caine.<br /> <br /> It's only at the cost of their souls.<br /> <br /> If you believe in that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> The Judas Compact is essentially the key behind-the-scenes under-the-table deal that resulted in the transformation of Roads into Paths. It is one of the most important events in Sabbat history but kept completely secret from the rank and file. It is also one of the most cynical and successful acts ever done by the organization. In simple terms, the Judas Compact was a rewriting of the literature of the Roads as well as their teachings in order to benefit the Sabbat. Large chunks of Kindred spirituality were completely destroyed, fake passages of the Book of Nod were created, and pamphlets for &quot;Priests&quot; of the Sabbat were created that were designed to essentially serve as &quot;how to&quot; manuals for manipulating packs into religiously throwing themselves into the jaws of their enemies.<br /> <br /> Getting into the nitty gritty of what was done would take days but some basic principles were set out that would come to dominate the Sabbat for centuries to come:<br /> <br /> * Caine is at war with the Antediluvians and wants you to destroy the latter as well as their minions.<br /> * The Antediluvian's minions are the Camarilla but also any vampire who is not Sabbat.<br /> * Diablerie is permissible, even lauded, in the pursuit of fighting the Antediluvian's minions.<br /> * Mass Embrace and killing of your own kind is permissible, even lauded, as long as it strengthens the holy war. You owe nothing to your cannon fodder until they prove themselves.<br /> * All Roads/Paths of Enlightenment are subordinate to the Sabbat's greater goals as the latter's truisms are perfect as well as unquestionable.<br /> * Each of the Roads/Paths must be modified to make sure that they divorce a follower from making any sort of compromise or peaceful interaction with humans. Separating vampires from mortal ties as well as morality is vital.<br /> * The Sabbat is fundamentally anti-mortal religion and any traditional faith or morality is to stamped out.<br /> <br /> The reasoning for this is unclear as all of the initial conspirators were deep believers in their own particular paths as well as Moncada being a fanatically faithful Catholic. Nevertheless, the three conspirators recruited others to join them as well as made arrangements for their commands to be inserted into the work being conducted at the Black Monastary in 1666. Payoffs were made, assassinations, mind-control, and several people actually persuaded that this was the best path forward for the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Immediate consequences for the Judas Compact were the following:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Road of Heaven, Road of Chivalry, and original Road of Night were effectively banned</b>: The latter two were warped beyond recognition by theologians at the Black Monastary with the former becoming the Road of Chivalry while the latter became a parody of its former self.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The Path of Caine was created, essentially, whole cloth as a scam religion: </b>Taking most of the principles and ideas of the Road of Blood, they were not shared among non-Assamites but used to brainwash new Kindred into their twisted version that was heretical to Alamut's followers but similar enough for work. The fact it attracted incredibly intelligent and scholarly Kindred was something that amused Sascha Vykos to no end over the centuries.<br /> <br /> 3.<b> The dividing of the Path of the Devil:</b> In exchange for Moncada's aid and connections in the Lasombra hierarchy, he insisted on the outlawing of the Path of the Devil. Most of the followers were converted to the Path of Cathari that kept its hedonistic freedom-loving ways while now worshiping the God beyond. Actual demon worshipers instead took to Inistar's Path of Evil Revelations that gained many followers in the wake of the obvious attempt to drive Road followers into cultish obedience.<br /> <br /> The Judas Compact was widely successful with most traditional Road followers either converting or paying lip service to the newly accepted Paths while carrying on their studies of their original faiths in private. The fundamental disconnect between the Paths as envisioned as a means of social control and &quot;vitae for the masses&quot; versus the real spiritual truths as well as belief by its members have been a source of discord in the Sabbat ever since.<br /> <br /> Many times, reform movements have sprung up among Kindred educated in the original Roads or who have figured out their own takes on the subject, but these have been stamped out as heresies. The Path of Evil Revelations was so much more effective at luring Sabbat hungry for truths (or power) that it was soon made into one of the most hated of all heretical faiths. To this day, there remains a diametrically opposed set of guidelines among Paths versus Roads as the former will always be crippled by the need for the Sword of Caine to control its minion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love it!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T17:54:01-08:00","id":1500983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1500955#post1500955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One is the role of the Ravnos Methusaleh Vestgeir in saving the sect in its early days, and the subsequent belief that Vestgeir was Caine in disguise. If you adopt that view, then it seems providential and provides a legitimacy to your new sect that it did not have before. And I'm sure one of the Path of Caine's tenants is &quot;Vestgeir was Caine&quot;, which would be unqiue to the Sabbat and not necessarily something that a non-Sabbat on the Path would have adopted. As players/fans, we are given very little information about Vestgeir's time with the Sabbat and his actions and words. But in the Sabbat this would have to be very important and well known. However, because mentions of Vestgeir seem limited to the 2e Sabbat books and does not seem to be mentioned in Revised source material, he is often not known and therefore people don't consider the importance he had in the sect. (Personally, I find it funny to consider that much of the Sabbat culture might be a result of a Ravnos con job). In so far that the Anarchs who only wanted freedom became Sabbat obsessed about the Antedeluvians, I think Vestgeir must have played a very important role in that transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me how we know nothing of Markel de Vesquel Itzal, the first Regent. I mean, the few things we know is that he is a Lasombra; he didn't approve the massacre of Silchester perpetrated by Sascha Vykos, think it too rash; he served as Regent for 100 years and then resigned (the only Regent to ever done so, and not be destroyed). So, in these early years I assume Sabbat was getting really organized by this more calm down-to-earth dude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T13:25:44-08:00","id":1501049,"title":"","content":"How many of you players have you used the path of the enlightenments at all. Or even the roads from the dark ages at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T15:02:22-08:00","id":1501068,"title":"","content":"Im guessing the Sabbat would try to purge paths of enligtenment such as Harmony, Self-Focus, and Scorched Heart, since these paths promote independance and critical thinking, something the sabbat doesent seem to want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T15:36:34-08:00","id":1501073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501049#post1501049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many of you players have you used the path of the enlightenments at all. Or even the roads from the dark ages at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>They've been present in a lot of my games and all dark age games I've ever played or run. I've personally played, power, honerable accord and bones.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cool trick a gm I know tends to run is you can't start of a path but you can join them in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T20:12:57-08:00","id":1501097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501049#post1501049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many of you players have you used the path of the enlightenments at all. Or even the roads from the dark ages at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've used Paths of Enlightenment in nine out of ten of the games I've run over the past three decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T09:44:43-08:00","id":1501145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1500877#post1500877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I in fact mention how strange it is for him to be and that was why I included him. Because in the WOD, I think you always need someone acting out of character sometimes because:<br /> <br /> 1. Vampires are innately hypocritical and will often do something against seemingly deeply held principles for power or control<br /> <br /> 2. They're not fully of their right mind when doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I would use someone with True Faith and a history of being against the Chruch of Caine in its entirely to be the mouth piece to show that Vampires can be hypocritical and not right of mind. That seems like just like using that character for the shock of it rather then something they would actually do. It doesn't make me think about how vampires can be hypnotical creatures, it just makes me lose verisimilitude of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T12:05:22-08:00","id":1501155,"title":"","content":"As it been pointed out in Children by Night. Moncada faith became dark and twisted and I can think how he could rationalize his actions and I seem to recall in Dark Ages Europe is that he is described as pragmatic and is willing to deal with his enemies if it serves his interests. I would like to see in future lore of how Moncada became the monster he would become in the modern nights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T16:09:41-08:00","id":1501177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501145#post1501145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I would use someone with True Faith and a history of being against the Chruch of Caine in its entirely to be the mouth piece to show that Vampires can be hypocritical and not right of mind. That seems like just like using that character for the shock of it rather then something they would actually do. It doesn't make me think about how vampires can be hypnotical creatures, it just makes me lose verisimilitude of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, he's a vampire with True Faith who was a key figure in the Path of Night that is as overtly evil as the Path of Typhon.<br /> <br /> In my write-up, I think it's suggested Moncada did this deal to target the Path of the Devil's followers in the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T23:21:07-08:00","id":1501216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501177#post1501177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, he's a vampire with True Faith who was a key figure in the Path of Night that is as overtly evil as the Path of Typhon.<br /> <br /> In my write-up, I think it's suggested Moncada did this deal to target the Path of the Devil's followers in the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is weird because he's on power and inner voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T09:31:54-08:00","id":1501241,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly (not something much guaranteed) Mon\u00e7ada was actually not a very good fan of Path of Night. It is attributed that he was some sort of inspiration or icon by the followers, but he himself wasn't a supporter of it. I love Ambrosio, but sometimes the character feels like its just wiggled around. The entire Clan Lasombra feels like that. Like Lucita is different in every book and novel in a way, but not in a in-universe manner. But you know, it could be interesting if Mon\u00e7ada worked to expand the Path of Night, but uses it as a tool for bigger means.<br /> <br /> Which reminds how Fabrizio Ulfila is a very cool Ventrue, that gets no spotlight. I imagine Ulfila and Mon\u00e7ada being part-time rivals, part-time allies. Mon\u00e7ada hated the Cainite Heresy, and I would assume Fabrizio would too. As much as they would fight to 'rule' the Catholic Church, they would also join powers against its enemies. <br /> <br /> Other thing. As Mon\u00e7ada hated the Church of Caine, it would make sense for him to have meddled with the Path of Caine. Which has lots of basis on the Heresy. Either a spiteful meddling that perverts the Path, or a calculated manipulation of a known enemy's philosophy. <br /> And one other speck, is how Mon\u00e7ada contacted Myca Vykos back in the 12-13th century, asking for him to kill Dracon. And Vykos sent the methuselah's signet, after the whole Archbishop Nikita/Dracon debacle. So they started working early. <br /> <br /> <br /> Velya is another cool character that gets little things to do. Being the wizened, less impulsive and more calculating of the Anarch Tzimisce Triunvirate (Vykos, Velya and Lugoj). And he is like the greatest authority on Metamorphism after Yorak got Cathedrald; besides being a top koldun first and foremost. I've always found strange how he just vanishes, then goes to Boston and has a very limited and personal little story, starts to degrade in the Path and thats it. <br /> Besides, its weird how the Eldest got Lugoj, but his two old-time comrades didn't notice anything strange afterwards. I guess he went to torpor after the diablerie, saying he would be back, and they let him snooze. Even when Lambach started crying wolf later-on. Seems like Vykos only started snooping around in Becket's Jyhad Diary. <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T11:25:12-08:00","id":1501250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501216#post1501216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is weird because he's on power and inner voice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure it's a bit like Vykos being on Death and Soul not Metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> It didn't exist yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T11:33:02-08:00","id":1501251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501250#post1501250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I figure it's a bit like Vykos being on Death and Soul not Metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> It didn't exist yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just took it that they showed how characters can have complex personalities and motivations outside of path membership same with vykos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T11:59:43-08:00","id":1501253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501068#post1501068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im guessing the Sabbat would try to purge paths of enligtenment such as Harmony, Self-Focus, and Scorched Heart, since these paths promote independance and critical thinking, something the sabbat doesent seem to want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree that Path Of Harmony wouldn't be welcome in the Sabbat as it does encourage a degree of empathy and some degree of humanity that is absent in that sect. Path of Self-Focus is a rare path and I can't see it ever being widely followed in general and probably would be viewed in the same light as the Path of Harmony. Path Of Scorched Heart I can't really comment on that much and I ignore it because I don't care for the True Brujah line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T14:52:41-08:00","id":1501267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501253#post1501253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Path Of Scorched Heart I can't really comment on that much and I ignore it because I don't care for the True Brujah line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Path of the scorched heart would have been a great camarlla path since it focuses on critical thinking, keeping a cool head, and leaving no stone unturned. A vampire who cant be emotionally manipulated sounds like quite a dangerous foe, or a very dependable ally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T16:06:37-08:00","id":1501275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501267#post1501267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Path of the scorched heart would have been a great camarlla path since it focuses on critical thinking, keeping a cool head, and leaving no stone unturned. A vampire who cant be emotionally manipulated sounds like quite a dangerous foe, or a very dependable ally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it would be a good Camarilla Path. The thing you'll need to ask for that is: How does this help Camarilla Elders hold or increase their power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T17:08:07-08:00","id":1501280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501275#post1501275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if it would be a good Camarilla Path. The thing you'll need to ask for that is: How does this help Camarilla Elders hold or increase their power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely following a path that focuses on critical thinking and eliminating every emotion you have would turn the elders into monsters almost immune to the manipulations of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T21:38:01-08:00","id":1501298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501253#post1501253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can agree that Path Of Harmony wouldn't be welcome in the Sabbat as it does encourage a degree of empathy and some degree of humanity that is absent in that sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is only true if you want the Sabbat to be some monolithic entity that tolerates no dissent. That is how it's been portrayed since Revised, but it is not the sect as originally presented in 2e. There were lots of Loyalists. Lots of Sabbat who represented something identifiable with the original Anarchs (like the Ventrue anti-tribu Dominique Touraine in Children of the Inquisition. Lots of Sabbat whose membership in the Sabbat was simply an artifact of the Sabbat getting to North America first and thus embracing the first vampires (The Path of Harmony was heavily based on the Country Gangrel, and was implied to be lots of vampires from Native American mortal stock who approached their condition from the beliefs of their mortal cultures and not those of European culture.) Lots of competing ideas in the sect.<br /> <br /> Personally I prefer the heavily divided Sabbat that seemed to be on the cusp of a Fourth Sabbat Civil War, and one where the Brujah anti-tribu (and their allies, the Ventrue anti-tribu!) were practically the equal of the Lasombra and Tzimisce, to the Revised-era depiction. It offered more flexibility to STs to portray the Sabbat to their needs of their chronicle, and offered many more tools so they could do so. Revised wanted to take away those tools so only the view of the Developer (Justin Achilli) were valid in order to sell the sourcebooks heavily based on metaplot rather than ST agency.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T23:07:47-08:00","id":1501301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501298#post1501298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Revised wanted to take away those tools so only the view of the Developer (Justin Achilli) were valid in order to sell the sourcebooks heavily based on metaplot rather than ST agency.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair to revised it did open up play options for Sabbat with members on humanity and fleshed out a lot of antitribu.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T23:29:03-08:00","id":1501303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501298#post1501298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revised wanted to take away those tools so only the view of the Developer (Justin Achilli) were valid in order to sell the sourcebooks heavily based on metaplot rather than ST agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, standard procedure with Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T01:30:25-08:00","id":1501306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501280#post1501280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Surely following a path that focuses on critical thinking and eliminating every emotion you have would turn the elders into monsters almost immune to the manipulations of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Entirely possible. I know far to little about the Path's details to be sure, only that the Camarilla don't seem to, to my understanding, exist for any other ultimate purpose than keeping the power with the Elders.<br /> <br /> And in all honestly I was more thinking of the Path disseminating among both Ancillae and Fledglings rather than strictly existing among the Elders of the sect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501298#post1501298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is only true if you want the Sabbat to be some monolithic entity that tolerates no dissent. That is how it's been portrayed since Revised, but it is not the sect as originally presented in 2e. There were lots of Loyalists. Lots of Sabbat who represented something identifiable with the original Anarchs (like the Ventrue anti-tribu Dominique Touraine in Children of the Inquisition. Lots of Sabbat whose membership in the Sabbat was simply an artifact of the Sabbat getting to North America first and thus embracing the first vampires (The Path of Harmony was heavily based on the Country Gangrel, and was implied to be lots of vampires from Native American mortal stock who approached their condition from the beliefs of their mortal cultures and not those of European culture.) Lots of competing ideas in the sect.<br /> <br /> Personally I prefer the heavily divided Sabbat that seemed to be on the cusp of a Fourth Sabbat Civil War, and one where the Brujah anti-tribu (and their allies, the Ventrue anti-tribu!) were practically the equal of the Lasombra and Tzimisce, to the Revised-era depiction. It offered more flexibility to STs to portray the Sabbat to their needs of their chronicle, and offered many more tools so they could do so. Revised wanted to take away those tools so only the view of the Developer (Justin Achilli) were valid in order to sell the sourcebooks heavily based on metaplot rather than ST agency.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest while I love most of Justin's work, VtM Revisited and VtR 1ed are my favorite Vampire editions, I do really like the description of the Sabbat that you lay out here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T11:13:04-08:00","id":1501328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501267#post1501267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Path of the scorched heart would have been a great camarlla path since it focuses on critical thinking, keeping a cool head, and leaving no stone unturned. A vampire who cant be emotionally manipulated sounds like quite a dangerous foe, or a very dependable ally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree on that basis of them being dangerous as they would have no issues on removing a problem that impedes them and the downside if I recall is that they don't really trust anyone even long time mates.<br /> <br /> At Black Fox thanks for sharing some of the additional info about how the Sabbat changed from each edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-25-2023, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T14:55:44-08:00","id":1501348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501328#post1501328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree on that basis of them being dangerous as they would have no issues on removing a problem that impedes them and the downside if I recall is that they don't really trust anyone even long time mates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldnt say they dont trust, more like they dont like to depend too much on others. The level 9 sin for scorched heart is &quot;relying on others&quot;, with the rationale being &quot;Your actions are the only ones you can predict with certainty.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T20:59:49-08:00","id":1501369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501303#post1501303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, standard procedure with Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think people are somewhat overly critical of Revised when it comes to issues of the Sabbat as they aren't really critical of the Sabbat in Revised, they're instead supportive of a Sabbat that isn't exactly the one that was in Second Edition.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat in Revised are overtly and openly evil, embracing their soccer hooligan status and doing all sorts of nasty things that are done for the sake of being nasty. However, the Sabbat in 2nd Edition still had that as a facet of a lot of Paths of Enlightenment's hierarchy of sins.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, it should be noted that Justin Achilli was the guy who changed the Sabbat from being massively and heavily infiltrated by Satanists/Infernalists to the point a major faction of the organization existed solely to stamp out the constant outbreaks of demon worship. Whenever people talk about the Sabbat before Revised, they basically try to ignore the fact demons were ruling it.<br /> <br /> I think if not for Montreal by Night, most Sabbat fans would prefer to get rid of the whole infernalism angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T21:13:19-08:00","id":1501371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501369#post1501369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think people are somewhat overly critical of Revised when it comes to issues of the Sabbat as they aren't really critical of the Sabbat in Revised, they're instead supportive of a Sabbat that isn't exactly the one that was in Second Edition.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat in Revised are overtly and openly evil, embracing their soccer hooligan status and doing all sorts of nasty things that are done for the sake of being nasty. However, the Sabbat in 2nd Edition still had that as a facet of a lot of Paths of Enlightenment's hierarchy of sins.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, it should be noted that Justin Achilli was the guy who changed the Sabbat from being massively and heavily infiltrated by Satanists/Infernalists to the point a major faction of the organization existed solely to stamp out the constant outbreaks of demon worship. Whenever people talk about the Sabbat before Revised, they basically try to ignore the fact demons were ruling it.<br /> <br /> I think if not for Montreal by Night, most Sabbat fans would prefer to get rid of the whole infernalism angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. It doesn't change that the Revised era of World of Darkness in general was typified by a significant curtailing of playstyles. As if to say, &quot;you are playing the game wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> People are capable of both changing ideas that didn't quite work, AND ALSO being very controlling about how players/storytellers engage with the games. The one does not excuse the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T01:56:40-08:00","id":1501385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501369#post1501369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think people are somewhat overly critical of Revised when it comes to issues of the Sabbat as they aren't really critical of the Sabbat in Revised, they're instead supportive of a Sabbat that isn't exactly the one that was in Second Edition.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat in Revised are overtly and openly evil, embracing their soccer hooligan status and doing all sorts of nasty things that are done for the sake of being nasty. However, the Sabbat in 2nd Edition still had that as a facet of a lot of Paths of Enlightenment's hierarchy of sins.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, it should be noted that Justin Achilli was the guy who changed the Sabbat from being massively and heavily infiltrated by Satanists/Infernalists to the point a major faction of the organization existed solely to stamp out the constant outbreaks of demon worship. Whenever people talk about the Sabbat before Revised, they basically try to ignore the fact demons were ruling it.<br /> <br /> I think if not for Montreal by Night, most Sabbat fans would prefer to get rid of the whole infernalism angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fundamental misreading of Revised Sabbat. The alien morality rationales are actually better established as the paths are cleaned up and refined. culture was elaborated as was ideology and mo. Re read the enlightenment paths in Revised era and mightnight siege vs 2nd ed or modern.<br /> <br /> I think think they downplay the demon worship because it's fundemently boring imo and doesn't really contribute much to the setting. Nephandi, pentex and baali did it better. Sabbat works better as a vampire supremacist movement.<br /> <br /> i honestly have no idea were youre getting football hooligan from. It's a genuine headscratcher, anarchs and v5 sabbat are probably closer and that's a hell of a stretch in off itself. Their arnt any irl equivelants to the Sabbat the closest is groups like Isis or ultra nationalist movement were morality is so alien as to be evil. A closer equivelant is something like mordor, the racist elves from skyrim or some of the chaos factions in 40k. We're morality is so bizzare and praxis so monstrous as to ultimatly just evil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 01-26-2023, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T09:11:55-08:00","id":1501409,"title":"","content":"I've been reading the Blood and Fire (Black Monastery specifically) chronicle, as well as Paths material these weeks, and it is interesting how you can sort of spread all the Sabbat Paths in four general schools. A more supreme hunter angle (with Caine's and Feral Heart Paths); an erudite study-focused one (with Death and Soul, Metamorphosis and even Bones if it was in Sabbat); a knight-honor-feudal school (Honorable Accord, Retribution, Inner Voice); and at last a licentious liberty group (Cathari, Revelation, Sin...), many of which actually would end up getting really close if not deep in Infernalism. These last Paths are similar in practice, but their beliefs and final goals are quite variant. <br /> <br /> Interesting as well, how Vykos was in the Road of Sin and then (supposedly sometime after the Dracon-mesh) started to follow the Death and Soul. Which I kind of think works better for them than the Metamorphosis one, cuz Death and Soul is about understanding and projects. Metamorphosis is way more self-center, its about transcendence, not a domination of the world by vampire masters. Also strange how Vykos embraced the faith in Caine in the Sabbat, even when Myca and Dracon were both very skeptical, and the latter was jaded as all hell. <br /> <br /> <br /> I also believe that initially, when the Sabbat formed proper - which I think should have some sort of event (in my setting I devised the Declaration of Majorca, based on the canon material) counter to the first Conclave and Convention of Thorns - it was WAY more secretive, it had lots of undercover agents, it was dense packed with the most powerful and faithful. The ones that didn't accept (or wouldn't get) amnesty from the Anarch War. So it was only with the spread over America that they began to get more numbers-heavy, and being capable of holding territory. <br /> But, new recruits, since the beginning, would be pretty idealistic or with few other choices. And like any good cult, they would be indoctrinated, alienated and integrated; any contact and bonds with their old unlife would be cut, if the sect couldn't exploit it. There wasn't many options... So, the Judas Compact would certainly have a great ground for their manipulated ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T17:06:23-08:00","id":1501441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500430-world-building-the-judas-compact-or-how-the-sabbat-got-their-groove-stolen?p=1501369#post1501369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, it should be noted that Justin Achilli was the guy who changed the Sabbat from being massively and heavily infiltrated by Satanists/Infernalists to the point a major faction of the organization existed solely to stamp out the constant outbreaks of demon worship. Whenever people talk about the Sabbat before Revised, they basically try to ignore the fact demons were ruling it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not how I would categorize it. As written the Sabbat was rife with infernalism with many leaders, including some Prisci and Archbishops, being secret members. But that is not the same as them leading the sect. They were clearly not in power. I always interpreted it as they were there in order to provide an internal enemy that the PCs could encounter and fight. They were there as someone who could fill the same role as the Sabbat does in a Camarilla chronicle: a dangerous bogeyman to be paranoid about.<br /> <br /> (I also think it was included as a call out to the old Hammer Horror movies where vampirism and Satanism went closely hand in hand.)<br /> <br /> The actual extent of infernalism within the sect or its relevance to a chronicle was always dependent on the taste of the individual ST. It's like how much of early VtM would make mention of blood-borne diseases as something that could harm vampires. Almost everyone I know ignored that because it didn't make sense to us that a corpse could be negatively affected by a disease. Players and STs who wanted to ignore that element could easily do so. It was just another tool for the ST.<br /> <br /> So no player ever needed Justin Achilli to come in and remove it, if they didn't feel comfortable with that as a setting element. Once again, it's just Justin arbitrarily deciding that because he didn't like something it needed to be removed from the game and take away a tool for the ST.<br /> <br /> I never put a figure of infernalists within the sect. But I would have placed them well under ten percent, even under five percent. Maybe something like three percent. It's just that infernalism would be concentrated in certain areas (where there was a coven) and so would be non-existent in others. It was just that the people most likely to turn to infernalism were ambitious, and the powers they gained from their infernalism would help them gain power, so an infernalist would be more likely to be rising within the sect's hierarchy rather than being one of the schmucks.<br /> <br /> So it was a noteworthy feature of the sect, but not necessarily a defining one. Others might imagine it differently, but that is OK. It was just another tool for the ST to use however she liked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}